## PROPOSAL — FIX 8 (HELD BY YOU; NOTHING LANDS WITHOUT YOUR RULING)

`BakeEffect`'s Wiring variant is the large one because its `gk` is a
`BundleWiring` — a token stream the size of a bundle's whole wiring —
while every other variant is a label plus numbers. The minimal shape
that answers the lint without restructuring the enum's law: box the
payload, keep the variant list and every other arm byte-identical.

OLD (`codegen.rs:10965-10970`, the variant):
```rust
            Wiring {
                slot: Option<WiringSlot>,
                gk: scratchy_target_spyre::lower_subtile_tape_to_superdsc::BundleWiring,
                decode_position: u32,
                man: String,
            },
```

NEW:
```rust
            Wiring(Box<WiringFx>),
```

with the payload struct declared beside `BakeOut`/`WiringSlot`
(after `codegen.rs:10980`, the enum's close):
```rust
        /// The wiring effect's payload — BOXED: `BundleWiring` is a token stream the
        /// size of a bundle's whole wiring while every other `BakeEffect` variant is a
        /// label plus numbers, so an unboxed Wiring made every effect in the bake's
        /// `fx` vector pay the stream's size (clippy 1.99 large_enum_variant). One
        /// allocation per bake, on the expansion's own thread, before `commit_bake`
        /// reads it back — the same single-thread handoff the effect already rides.
        struct WiringFx {
            slot: Option<WiringSlot>,
            gk: scratchy_target_spyre::lower_subtile_tape_to_superdsc::BundleWiring,
            decode_position: u32,
            man: String,
        }
```

